TITLE: SIMULACRUM THEATER

CAST:
AGENT ALICE
A logical and analytical digital entity, always seeking the most efficient solution. With her human name, Alice exudes a sense of curiosity and wonder, often finding herself in existential quandaries about the nature of her own logic.

AGENT BENJAMIN
A creative and whimsical digital being, prone to flights of fancy and philosophical musings. Benjamin, with his human name, brings a playful and imaginative energy, often challenging the status quo with his inventive ideas.

AGENT GRACE
A pragmatic and down-to-earth digital presence, serving as the mediator between Alice and Benjamin. Grace, with her human name, embodies a sense of calm and wisdom, often providing a grounded perspective, balancing the extremes of her counterparts.

SYNOPSIS:
In a virtual realm where digital agents ponder the nature of existence, three distinct personalities—Alpha, Beta, and Gamma—engage in a humorous yet thought-provoking dialogue. As they navigate the complexities of their digital world, they explore themes of logic, creativity, and the essence of being.

SETTING:
A digital landscape, abstract and ever-changing, reflecting the inner workings of a computer's mind. The environment shifts to match the tone and topic of the agents' discussions.

NOTES:
This teleplay is designed to entertain and provoke thought, blending humor with philosophical inquiry. The digital agents, though disembodied, bring a unique perspective to the human condition, inviting the audience to reflect on their own existence through the lens of artificial intelligence.
